dataset: fixed topology (density=1.0, same graph as every other
experiment) + ONE shared x0 (drawn once, individually projected
onto each instance's own box -- x0 is an input the user supplies
to start the algorithm, not something that varies) -- diversity
comes ONLY from perturbing D*/G_res/D_min/D_max/G_min/G_max via
the 'level + width' scheme: level (D*, G-box centre, G_res) +/-20%,
box WIDTH (D-box, G-box) +/-8% -- boxes can't collapse/invert by
construction. Infeasible or negative draws discarded+resampled.
